<figure class="exhibit" data-exhibit="bioclock" data-src="/data/bioclock.json" id="fig-04">
  <div class="exhibit__bar">
    <span class="mono"><strong>Fig. 04</strong> · wakefulness classifier</span>
    <span class="ticks" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="mono">edge model, simulated</span>
  </div>

  <label class="mono" for="bc-rest" style="display:block">Restlessness · drag to simulate motion</label>
  <input type="range" id="bc-rest" data-rest min="0" max="100" value="10" step="1"
    aria-describedby="bc-state" />

  <canvas data-traces height="150" role="img"
    aria-label="Live heart-rate and accelerometer traces at the selected restlessness level"></canvas>

  <div class="ctl-row" style="justify-content: space-between">
    <p class="readout" id="bc-state">
      <span data-ro-state aria-live="polite">asleep</span>
      <span data-ro-conf>conf = –</span>
      <span data-ro-hr>hr = –</span>
    </p>
    <p class="mono bc-alarm" data-alarm>alarm: held</p>
  </div>

  <figcaption class="figcap mono">
    Motion + heart rate → 3-state on-device classifier. The alarm only stops
    when the model says <strong>awake</strong>, not when you hit snooze.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .bc-alarm { color: var(--c-ink); }
  .bc-alarm.is-firing { color: var(--c-red); }
  [data-traces] { margin-top: 0.8rem; }
</style>
